DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     A drawing set lives for years, and the questions the shop
     asks about it - what it takes, where anything is, what a
     library holds and what the set contains - vveelliinnffoo answers.
     These are the shell's questions, not the window's, and their
     natural asker is mmaakkee(1).

     Two of the four answer in prose on standard output and two
     answer with an ordinary DRAWING - which is the point: a
     drawing is the format the rest of the suite already prints,
     so a generated card goes to paper with no new backend and no
     temporary file.  The file name - is standard input.

     -lleenn
     The TAKEOFF.  Wires, connectors and polylines are measured
     in sheet units, per NET where the conductors have names and
     per LAYER otherwise, with a set total.  H-V routes measure
     both legs; diagonals measure an integer square root.

     A closed FILLED polyline reports AREA instead - integer
     shoelace, halved, with the odd half shown as ``.5'' - be-
     cause sheet metal is ordered by area the way cable is or-
     dered by length.

     A set whose sheets disagree about the UU unit is refused in
     one line rather than adding millimetres to inches.  (That
     disagreement is also a vveellcchheecckk finding, which is where a
     build should catch it.)

     -wwhheerree
     The set-wide Find: a case-blind substring over designators,
     values, text and net names - the editor's Find contract re-
     stated over FILES - one line per hit with the grid position.
     The EXIT STATUS is the hit count.

     Zero hits exits 0 silently, so the INVERTED use is free:
     vveelliinnffoo -wwhheerree TTOODDOO *.dd in a cchheecckk: rule fails the build
     while a sheet still carries a TODO note.

     -ssyymmsshheeeett
     The library ON PAPER: a grid of every stencil in ONE .ssyymm
     file with its code, designator prefix and pin types, emitted
     as an ordinary drawing, so the shop's binder fills itself
     from make:

                  velinfo -symsheet pid.sym | velplot -T ps -fit -


