     The card names its stencils by CODE like any drawing, so
     whatever reads it back must have that library loaded: put a
     library of your own in /usr/vellum/etc/libs first.

     -bbooookk
     The set as a DOCUMENT: an ordinary drawing listing the
     sheets given - number, file name, and the sheet's own title,
     which it takes from the first text object on the FRAME layer
     (where the frame stamp puts $FF, so a stamped set titles it-
     self), falling back to the largest text on the sheet and
     then to the file name.

     It is .dd out, so it prints on every device, vveellpplloott -ttiillee ss
     if it has to, and opens in the editor when somebody wants to
     fix a title by hand:

                  velinfo -book amp?.d > contents.d
                  velplot -T ps contents.d amp?.d | lpr

     The sheets stay FILES.  A book is a contents drawing plus a
     shell glob in the right order, not a container format.

